# Partita No. 1 in B-flat major, BWV 825: Praeludium (J. S. Bach)
#
# Identification: Mutopia's Partita 1 set (Clavierubung I) is numbered
# by movement; 11title-hub is movement 1, headed "1. Praeludium" in the
# score (11hub.ly), 21 bars of 4/4 in B-flat. Confirmed.
#
# Character: the gentle, singing opening of the first published Partita
# (1726/1731). Three voices: a melody built from a short turn figure
# (B-flat, a quick mordent-like turn, then stepping eighths and
# sixteenths), with flowing thirty-second-note turns passed between the
# hands. Calm and lyrical, never rushed; four beats to the bar.
#
# Time signature: 4/4, 21 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI, no
# upbeat, no repeats (the Praeludium has none). The last bar is a
# B-flat chord under a fermata.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 44, about 2:00.
# Track times: Glenn Gould (Sony) 1:52 to 1:53, about quarter = 45;
# Andras Schiff (live recording) 1:52 in one listing, about 45 (the same
# figure as Gould, so possibly a listing error); Eleonor Bindman (Delos)
# 2:28, about 34. 44 follows Gould and Schiff. At 44 a thirty-second is
# about 10 frames, so the turns stay distinct on the chip; slower, the
# long notes would fade.
#
# Structure (read from the Mutopia score; my reading):
#   1-2     the turn figure, top, B-flat, over a held B-flat in the bass.
#   3-4     thirty-second-note turns rising in sequence.
#   4-6     the figure in the bass, on F; move to F major.
#   7-8     the turns in the bass under suspensions above.
#   9-10    the figure in the middle voice, on D (G minor).
#   11-13   the figure in the top on C; cadence in F major (13-14).
#   14-16   the turns in the bass, back toward B-flat.
#   17-18   the figure in the bass on F, the dominant pedal region.
#   19-20   the figure in the top again in B-flat (= bars 1-2), a tenor
#           added below for a fuller close.
#   21      final chord, fermata.
#
# Plan: no repeats, so the shape comes from the entries of the figure.
# mf for the opening; a step down (mp) when the figure moves into the
# middle voice and minor keys (9-13); back to mf from the F cadence;
# full (f) for the return in 19 with the added tenor. Each entry of the
# figure in an inner or lower voice brought forward. Breadth only at
# the F major cadence and at the end.

tempo 44

dyn 1 mf           # 1-8: the opening, B-flat to F
lead 4-5 bottom    # the figure in the bass, on F
dyn 9 mp           # 9-13: the figure in the middle voice, G minor
lead 9 mid         # the figure on D in the middle voice
lead 12 top        # the figure on C in the top
broaden 13 0.94    # into the F major cadence
dyn 14 mf          # 14-18: the bass leads back to B-flat
lead 17-18 bottom  # the figure in the bass on F
dyn 19 f           # 19-21: the return, with the added tenor

rit 2 0.6          # the last two bars into the fermata
